Description: pass CustomTarget objects in ssc_server depends
 Meson 1.4.2 (Ubuntu 24.04) rejects CustomTargetIndex entries in
 custom_target(depends:). python_gen stored protobuf_python_gen[0], and
 depends: [python_gen] flattened to an array of CustomTargetIndex, so
 libssc failed at configure time on the Ubuntu 24.04 build baseline.
 .
 Store the CustomTarget itself and pass the array directly.
Origin: self
Author: GhfunNiHe <131235947+GhfunNiHe@users.noreply.github.com>
Forwarded: no
--- a/mocking/ssc_server/meson.build
+++ b/mocking/ssc_server/meson.build
@@ -47,7 +47,7 @@
     install: true,
     install_dir: [join_paths(python.get_install_dir(), 'ssc_server')]
   )
-  python_gen += protobuf_python_gen[0]
+  python_gen += [protobuf_python_gen]
 endforeach
 
 # Make the SSC Server available during tests
@@ -57,7 +57,7 @@
   output: ['qmi.py', 'ssc.py', 'ssc-server', 'ssc-server-tests'],
   command: ['cp', '@INPUT@', '@OUTDIR@'],
   build_by_default: true,
-  depends: [python_gen]
+  depends: python_gen
 )
 
 subdir('data')
